#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1185
msgid ""
"Move what is to be private from the shareable disk to the private one, in "
"the file manager. It is then encrypted, and deleted from the shareable disk, "
"though the provider may keep the deleted version for a while. What is to be "
"shared stays where it is."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1189
msgid ""
"To share them, or to make them private, set up the shareable disk: Set Up "
"With rclone offers it. Then move what is to be private to the private disk, "
"in the file manager. It is then encrypted, and deleted from the shareable "
"disk, though the provider may keep the deleted version for a while."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1194
msgid ""
"The program moves nothing itself: what was shared with you, or what others "
"use, stays where it is until you move it."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1219
msgid "Asking the service…"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a cloud service, e.g. "Dropbox".
#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1260
#, c-format
msgid "Unencrypted Files at %s"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1262
#, c-format
msgid ""
"rclone encrypts what goes through the private disk, and keeps it in one "
"folder at %s. Anything else there, from before or put there another way, the "
"provider can read."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1266
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The program can ask %s how many files and folders lie outside the encrypted "
"folder. It asks over the network, with rclone and rclone's own login, and "
"only when you press the button. Only how many comes back: no names are kept "
"or shown."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: %s is a cloud service, e.g. "Dropbox".
#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1283 src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1523
#, c-format
msgid "Look at %s"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1315
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s looks like a file encrypted with its own password, such as a password "
"database. It is where %s gets it. It holds as well as its password does: "
"whoever has the file, the provider included, can try passwords against it as "
"many times as they like, without anyone noticing."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1319
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s looks like a key, a password or a stored login, and it is where %s gets "
"it. Whether the provider can read it depends on whether it is encrypted "
"before it leaves this computer, which cannot be seen from here."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1322
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%s looks like a key, a password or a stored login, and it is where %s gets "
"it. The provider can read what is sent there."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1326
msgid ""
"Move it to the private disk, in the file manager: the disk's encryption then "
"comes on top of its own, so the provider has nothing to try passwords "
"against. A private disk is set up with Set Up With rclone. The program moves "
"nothing itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1330
msgid ""
"Find out first, in the service's own settings, whether this folder is "
"encrypted before it leaves. If it is not, move the file out of the cloud "
"folder, or to the private disk, in the file manager. The program moves "
"nothing itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1334
msgid ""
"Move it out of the cloud folder, or to the private disk, in the file "
"manager. The program moves nothing itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1338
msgid ""
"The provider often keeps earlier versions and deleted files for a while, so "
"it may have this one already. Where the file holds a key or a password, "
"replacing it, with a new key or a changed password, is the way to be sure."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: the page's title.
#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1342
msgid "An Encrypted File in a Cloud Folder"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:1343
